-- Proven client-side consumer, read straight out of the decompiled
-- ClientFramework.Classes.GunClass rather than assumed:
--     GetSpreadModifier() : base = 1, or 2 without the "Basic FirearmsTraining" talent
--                           returns base + GetInfo("FirearmSpread")
--     GetSpread()         : returns MaxSpread * velocityFactor * GetSpreadModifier()
-- It is a MULTIPLIER TERM, not one of the additive bonuses the textboxes below use, so it is exposed
-- in percent. ⚠ THE RANGE GOES TO -200% ON PURPOSE: the base is 2 rather than 1 for anyone without
-- Basic FirearmsTraining, so -100% only cancels the talent penalty for them and -200% is what
-- actually reaches zero. Positive values widen spread.
--
-- Two things in that same file decide whether the slider appears to do ANYTHING:
--   * GetSpread returns 0 outright when HRP velocity <= 1 — standing still is already pinpoint, so
--     the slider can only be judged while MOVING.
--   * ApplySpread returns the direction unchanged when distance <= Range/2 — no spread is applied
--     at close range either.
-- Also note velocityFactor normalises by (20 + GetInfo("RunSpeed")), so the RunSpeed pin already
-- tightens gun accuracy as a side effect.
local fsSlider
fsSlider = secAck:Slider("Firearm Spread",
